RESULTS = """Yesterday’s UEFA Champions League action on Wednesday, November 25, 2026, delivered a thrilling slate of nine Matchday 5 fixtures across Europe, packed with dominant away victories, dramatic draws, and a major upset in France.

The evening kicked off with two early fixtures that both went the way of the Spanish visitors. In Baku, Barcelona put on a commanding display at the Baku Olympic Stadium, cruising past Sabah with a 4–1 victory to take all three points. Over in Prague, Villarreal had to work much harder for their win, grinding out a narrow 1–0 triumph over Slavia Prague at the Eden Aréna in a tense, physical contest that saw six yellow cards handed out.

When the later kickoffs rolled around, the headline shock of the night unfolded at the Stade Pierre-Mauroy, where LOSC Lille stunned German giants Bayern Munich with a massive 2–1 home victory. Elsewhere in France, Paris Saint-Germain and AS Roma played out a breathless 2–2 draw at the Parc des Princes. Roma struck first through Mario Hermoso in the 5th minute before Illya Zabarnyi leveled for PSG in the 31st; the second half was decided from the penalty spot, with Ousmane Dembélé putting the hosts ahead in the 62nd minute only for Donyell Malen to convert a 78th-minute penalty and salvage a point for the Italian side.

There was another high-drama 2–2 draw in Lisbon, where Sporting CP and Manchester United shared the spoils at the Estádio José Alvalade in a fiery encounter that ended with Manchester United picking up a stoppage-time red card via a second yellow in the 93rd minute. Meanwhile, Liverpool had no such trouble on their travels, dismantling Club Brugge 3–0 at the Jan Breydel Stadium with a clinical away performance.

In the remaining fixtures, Inter Milan took care of business at the San Siro, securing a comfortable 2–0 win over VfB Stuttgart. Atlético Madrid matched that scoreline at the Riyadh Air Metropolitano, defeating Viking 2–0 in a match where the Norwegian side was reduced to ten men by a stoppage-time red card. Finally, at Stamford Bridge in London, Fenerbahçe edged out Shakhtar Donetsk 1–0 to wrap up a memorable Wednesday night of Champions League football."""
